            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="0830" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2311: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-04T14:00:00+07:00">October 4, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 4—10:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>503. I perceive no objection to Butrick discussing the proposal contained in his
                    1025, October 3, 1 p.m. Until I am certain that the Chinese Government will not
                    give its consent to such a proceeding I must doubtless accept it if it were
                    found feasible and put into effect without involving the necessity of its
                    consent.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
